# Supply-chain hardening: refuse to install packages younger than 7 days.
# Catches the typical compromise pattern where an attacker publishes a
# trojaned version of a popular package — by the time we'd see it, the
# real maintainer has usually noticed and yanked it.
#
# Requires pnpm 10.16+. NOTE: pnpm interprets this value in MINUTES
# (unlike bun's minimumReleaseAge which is seconds). 7d × 24h × 60min
# = 10080.
minimum-release-age=10080
